oved by those amendments, would not make every practitioner an investigator. It would prohibit knowing participation in a particular and discriminatory practice. The fact that a bill can be improved in Committee is not an argument to defeat it at the second reading stage. It is an argument to pass the principle and do the drafting work properly.","result":"negative","slug":"division-nsw-lc-2026-09-16-4","source_url":"https://api.parliament.nsw.gov.au/api/hansard/search/daily/fragment/HANSARD-1820781676-105297"}
